by BenMorel at 2025-05-22T20:11:30Z

@stof Good point. `_fragment` was introduced in 2014, in 6d79a565e0e56b525134080687eba3961eab1a73, PR #12979, and was first released in `v3.2.0` — a minor release.

The BC break concern [was raised](https://github.com/symfony/symfony/pull/12979#issuecomment-66962833) by @Koc back then, but [was dismissed](https://github.com/symfony/symfony/pull/12979#issuecomment-72749346) by @Tobion:

> And the tiny BC break is negligible because it's unlikely.

I'll leave it up to you to decide whether introducing another one in a minor release is still acceptable in 2025; maybe this is something that could be documented in [Our Backward Compatibility Promise](https://symfony.com/doc/current/contributing/code/bc.html)?
